{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/5/codegen_prompts/2.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/5`\n- 题号：`2`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2131201979/5/2.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"2\">\n- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色碎片按颜色配对，每对碎片的重叠形状决定在两者之间的中点位置绘制何种填充图案。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为最常见颜色。\n  - 网格中存在若干对相同颜色的小型连通对象（每种非背景颜色恰好出现两个4-连通对象），每个对象占2–5个像素。\n  - 同色的两个对象形状可能不同：一个可能是另一个的子集，也可能彼此有部分重叠、部分差异。\n  - 网格边缘有一个由grey像素构成的小参考标记（例如一个2×2方块），用于指示输出图案的填充颜色为grey。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种颜色，找到该颜色的两个对象A和B。\n  - 将A和B各自裁剪到最小包围盒，左上角对齐后求像素交集（两者都有前景像素的位置）。\n  - 计算A和B包围盒中心的中点位置（取整），以该中点为左上角，用grey颜色绘制交集形状。\n  - 原始的彩色对象保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：同色两对象不是简单复制关系——需要对齐后取交集才能得到输出图案的形状，而图案的放置位置由两个对象的空间中点决定，形状与位置的信息来源完全不同。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/e9fc42f2, eval/332f06d7, train/aa62e3f4, train/f8cc533f, eval/bf45cf4b, eval/e87109e9, eval/dbff022c, eval/7b3084d4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e9fc42f2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3379\nmechanism=0.3750\nlexical=0.0144\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e9fc42f2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e9fc42f2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAssemble the foreground objects by docking equal-colored boundary markers edge-to-edge.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several 4-connected multicolor foreground\nobjects.  One foreground color is the body color; the less frequent foreground colors are\nboundary connector markers, and each marker color appears once as a free end or twice as a\nmatched docking pair.\n\nRule\nCrop each foreground object to its bounding box and translate the objects so that the two\noccurrences of every paired connector color touch on their exposed boundary sides.  Preserve\neach object's orientation and colors, then return the tight crop around the assembled\nforeground on the original background color.\n\nKey insight\nThe colored marker pixels are ports: matching colors specify which objects must touch, and\nthe marker's side of its object determines the direction of the translation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground object sprite s with boundary connector markers\",\n  \"dst\": \"matching boundary connector marker d on another sprite\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.marker.color and the two marker pixels have opposite exposed sides\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate sprites so each paired marker touches edge-to-edge; preserve sprite colors and orientation\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"tight crop of the assembled foreground on the original background color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2719\nmechanism=0.2947\nlexical=0.0146\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:marker, object:square, operation:flood_fill, output:same_size\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aa62e3f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3080\nmechanism=0.3306\nlexical=0.0158\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, output:same_size, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/aa62e3f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/aa62e3f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace the outlined object with the outside contour of that outline in the marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f8cc533f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2859\nmechanism=0.3456\nlexical=0.0145\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:aligned, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f8cc533f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f8cc533f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete every colored sprite by applying the union of all aligned partial sprite masks.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Each non-background color appears as a separated partial copy of one common sprite mask.\n- The copies share a top-left-aligned sprite window; some copies may be missing lower or right edge pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop each same-color mask to its bounding box.\n- Pad the crops to the maximum observed height and width, aligned at the top-left, and OR them into one complete template.\n- Fill that template at every sprite location using the sprite's own color.\n\nKey insight:\n- No single input sprite is complete, but their missing cells are complementary, so the aligned union reveals the full mask.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"same-color partial sprite masks, one per foreground color, sharing a top-left-aligned window\",\n  \"transform\": \"pad smaller masks down/right to the largest observed window, recover the complete sprite as the union of all aligned masks, then fill that mask in each sprite window using that window's color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"bf45cf4b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3041\nmechanism=0.3251\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:sprite, object:square, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/bf45cf4b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/bf45cf4b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nScale up a monochrome control sprite by stamping a polychrome tile at each filled pixel.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background color.\n- Two foreground objects (8-connected): a monochrome rectangular sprite with bg holes (control), and a polychrome square tile (block).\n\nRule:\n- For each cell in the control sprite's bbox: if filled, stamp a copy of the block tile; if bg, leave a tile-sized bg region.\n- Output grid dimensions are (control_h × tile_h) by (control_w × tile_w).\n\nKey insight: The control sprite acts as a binary mask that gets \"pixel-scaled\" by the tile — each pixel expands to a full tile copy or empty space.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"monochrome sprite\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
